type: Ruleset
version: v1
metadata:
    name: gomboc-ai/bicep/azure/Microsoft.Sql/securityAlertPolicies/ckv-azure-25-sql-threat-detection-types
    display_name: Enable All Threat Detection Types for Azure SQL Bicep
    skip: false
    priority: 1250000
    description: |
        ## Description

        Ensures that all threat detection alert types are enabled on Azure SQL Server security
        alert policies defined in Bicep templates.

        The `disabledAlerts` property on `securityAlertPolicies` resources is an array of threat
        category strings that are suppressed. When this array is non-empty, the corresponding
        alert types are silenced. This rule detects any non-empty `disabledAlerts` array and
        replaces it with `[]`, re-enabling all detection types.

        Both resource declaration patterns are covered:
        1. `Microsoft.Sql/servers/databases/securityAlertPolicies` — database-level policy.
        2. `Microsoft.Sql/servers/securityAlertPolicies` — server-level policy.
        3. Inline child resource `securityAlertPolicies@<version>` nested inside a parent
           `databases` resource block (Bicep parent/child inline syntax).

        ## Known Limitations

        - `disabledAlerts` specified as a parameter or variable reference (e.g.,
          `disabledAlerts: alertsParam`) is not matched — only literal arrays are captured.
        - The absent `disabledAlerts` property is treated as compliant (all alerts active by
          platform default).

        ## SCOPE_NOTE vs CKV_AZURE_25 (Checkov)

        Checkov CKV_AZURE_25 targets the Terraform runner
        (`azurerm_mssql_server_security_alert_policy.disabled_alerts`). For Bicep, Checkov
        processes templates via ARM JSON compilation or a dedicated Bicep runner. This ORL rule
        directly targets the Bicep AST and covers both database-level and server-level resource
        types, plus inline child syntax.

        Absent `disabledAlerts` is treated as **compliant** by this rule, consistent with the
        Azure platform default (all alerts enabled when the property is omitted). Checkov's exact
        behavior for absent `disabledAlerts` in Bicep is unconfirmed; scanner counts may differ.
    annotations:
        contributed-by: gomboc-ai
        gomboc-ai/checkov/id: CKV_AZURE_25
        gomboc-ai/checkov/name: Ensure that 'Threat Detection types' is set to 'All'
        gomboc-ai/configoption/capability/title: Enable All Threat Detection Types on Azure SQL Server (Bicep)
        gomboc-ai/description-plain: Ensures that all threat detection alert types are enabled on Azure SQL Server security alert policies by setting disabledAlerts to an empty array in Bicep templates.
        gomboc-ai/example: |-
            ```diff
            resource securityAlertPolicy 'Microsoft.Sql/servers/databases/securityAlertPolicies@2021-11-01' = {
              name: '${sqlDatabase.name}/default'
              properties: {
                state: 'Enabled'
            -   disabledAlerts: ['Sql_Injection', 'Data_Exfiltration']
            +   disabledAlerts: []
              }
            }
            ```
        gomboc-ai/future-improvements: Add support for detecting disabledAlerts set to [''] (single empty-string element), which some Checkov implementations treat as equivalent to disabling no alerts. Consider adding an audit-only variant that flags parameter-referenced disabledAlerts values for manual review.
        gomboc-ai/impact/score: low
        gomboc-ai/impact/statement: |
            ## Impact

            Sets `disabledAlerts` to `[]` on `Microsoft.Sql/servers/databases/securityAlertPolicies`
            and `Microsoft.Sql/servers/securityAlertPolicies` resources.
            * **Alert notifications** for previously suppressed threat categories will resume upon next deployment.
            * **No data loss** or schema changes occur; this only affects the Advanced Threat Protection notification configuration.
            * Enabling additional alert types may surface new alerts for previously undetected issues.
        gomboc-ai/impact/statement-plain: Sets disabledAlerts to [] on Microsoft.Sql/servers/databases/securityAlertPolicies and Microsoft.Sql/servers/securityAlertPolicies resources. This re-enables any previously suppressed alert types, causing alerts and notifications to be generated for those threat categories.
        gomboc-ai/limitations/application: This rule only applies when disabledAlerts is set to a literal non-empty array. If disabledAlerts is omitted entirely, the resource is considered compliant (Azure defaults to all alerts enabled). If disabledAlerts is set via a Bicep parameter or variable reference, the rule cannot statically resolve the value and will not match.
        gomboc-ai/limitations/implementation: 'Bicep parameter and variable references for disabledAlerts (e.g., disabledAlerts: alertsParam) cannot be statically resolved by ORL. Expression-valued disabledAlerts properties are out of scope. The rule relies on tree-sitter AST matching of literal array nodes only.'
        gomboc-ai/provider: Azure
        gomboc-ai/public-rule-bodies: "true"
        gomboc-ai/resource: Microsoft.Sql/servers/securityAlertPolicies
        gomboc-ai/reviewer/date: "2026-04-06"
        gomboc-ai/reviewer/name: matt.sweeney@gomboc.ai
        gomboc-ai/reviewer/status: valid
        gomboc-ai/risk/score: low
        gomboc-ai/risk/statement: |
            ## Risk

            Setting `disabledAlerts` to `[]` is a **non-destructive** template change.
            * Existing SQL databases and server configurations are not altered — only the Advanced Threat Protection alert suppression list is cleared.
            * Alert volume may increase as previously suppressed threat categories begin generating findings.
            * No downtime, resource recreation, or data migration is required.
        gomboc-ai/risk/statement-plain: Setting disabledAlerts to an empty array is a non-destructive change. It restores full threat monitoring by re-enabling all alert types. No SQL data or schema is affected.
        gomboc-ai/severity/score: medium
        gomboc-ai/severity/statement: |
            ## Severity

            Partially disabling threat detection creates monitoring blind spots on Azure SQL:
            * **SQL Injection** suppression allows injection attacks to proceed silently without alerts.
            * **Data Exfiltration** suppression hides unauthorized bulk data extraction activity.
            * **Access Anomaly** suppression conceals unusual login patterns indicative of credential compromise.
            * **Compliance**: Violates CKV_AZURE_25 (Prisma Cloud bc-azr-general-6) and reduces Azure Defender for SQL coverage.

            Remediation should occur promptly for any internet-facing SQL Server.
        gomboc-ai/severity/statement-plain: Disabling threat detection types creates monitoring blind spots that allow SQL injection attacks, data exfiltration, and other threats to go undetected. This violates CKV_AZURE_25 / Prisma Cloud bc-azr-general-6.
        gomboc-ai/visibility: public
        use-case-1: git@github.com:Gomboc-AI/orl-rules.git;main;/workspace/use-case-ff812b1d-202603152005/bicep/outputs/ckv-azure-25-sql-threat-detection-types-bicep
    classifications:
        - gomboc-ai/policy/surface_area/auditing_and_monitoring/security_logs
        - gomboc-ai/prismacloud/CKV_AZURE_25
spec:
    template:
        language: bicep
        audit_language: ast
        variables: []
        collect: []
        audit: ""
        remediation: []
    rules:
        - name: database-level-non-empty-disabled-alerts
          language: null
          variables: null
          audit: |
            (resource_declaration
              (string
                (string_content) @_type (#match? @_type "^Microsoft\\.Sql/servers/databases/securityAlertPolicies@")
              )
              (object
                (object_property
                  (identifier) @_props_key (#eq? @_props_key "properties")
                  (object
                    (object_property
                      (identifier) @_da_key (#eq? @_da_key "disabledAlerts")
                      (array
                        .
                        (string
                          (string_content) @_first_item
                        )
                      ) @da_value
                    )
                  )
                )
              )
            )
          remediation:
            - command: replace
              path: da_value
              skip: ""
              value: '[]'
              flags: {}
          collect: null
        - name: server-level-non-empty-disabled-alerts
          language: null
          variables: null
          audit: |
            (resource_declaration
              (string
                (string_content) @_type (#match? @_type "^Microsoft\\.Sql/servers/securityAlertPolicies@")
              )
              (object
                (object_property
                  (identifier) @_props_key (#eq? @_props_key "properties")
                  (object
                    (object_property
                      (identifier) @_da_key (#eq? @_da_key "disabledAlerts")
                      (array
                        .
                        (string
                          (string_content) @_first_item
                        )
                      ) @da_value
                    )
                  )
                )
              )
            )
          remediation:
            - command: replace
              path: da_value
              skip: ""
              value: '[]'
              flags: {}
          collect: null
        - name: inline-child-non-empty-disabled-alerts
          language: null
          variables: null
          audit: |
            (resource_declaration
              (string
                (string_content) @_type (#match? @_type "^securityAlertPolicies@")
              )
              (object
                (object_property
                  (identifier) @_props_key (#eq? @_props_key "properties")
                  (object
                    (object_property
                      (identifier) @_da_key (#eq? @_da_key "disabledAlerts")
                      (array
                        .
                        (string
                          (string_content) @_first_item
                        )
                      ) @da_value
                    )
                  )
                )
              )
            )
          remediation:
            - command: replace
              path: da_value
              skip: ""
              value: '[]'
              flags: {}
          collect: null
